<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonzalo de Alvarado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Gonzalo de Alvarado y Chávez</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonzalo de Alvarado was a Spanish conquistador and relative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a> who took part in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. In 1525 he besieged Zaculeu, the fortified capital of the Mam kingdom in the western highlands, for several months, until its starving defenders under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaibil-balam">Kaibil Balam</a> surrendered. The victory brought the Mam under Spanish rule.</p></div>
